Apply the virtual Linus Torvalds code-quality lens: dead code, logic holes (readHNSWOptions against parseConfig's order and defaults; hnswConfigChecks against Config's constructor; the maintainer's and the evolution check's use of the one reader, including aliases in the changed-options set; canonicalEntry's field encodings per kind; elementPriors' LCS, tie-break, content pass and position fallback; the per-walk reach), incomplete conversions, papered-over regressions, test assertions weakened or vacuous, claims in comments, CHANGELOG, DIVERGENCES and 7.16 wider than the code, and whether the evidence shows what 7.16 says it shows.
